 "name": "Glass Rollout Wave 2 — Profile shipped pairings, 2026-07-03",
 "_doc": [
  "Self-contained wave declaration for the Profile screen. Reuses the Tasks/Wave-1 shipped surfaces (row / banner / stage / ctaFill / chipOnStage) verbatim and ADDS chipOnRow (an engineered chip tint sitting on a row-glass card: the RecentlyViewed chips + the ReportsBreakdown total chip).",
  "Profile cards are in normal flow over the ScreenStage (never overlapping app content), so a row card's worst-case backdrop is the stage's darkest stops — the same bases Wave-1/Tasks used for `row`, NOT #000. Engineered rows (nav/about/siblings) carry a MORE opaque floor (rowLite 0.84/0.88) than the true-blur floor declared here (0.70/0.72), so declaring against the true-blur `row` floor is the conservative bound that covers both.",
  "New forks confirmed by this run: heroValue brand -> inkDetailsGhost (dark #84AEF6, raw brand fails on dark glass); point-delta gain successStrong(light)/success(dark) + loss error(light)/errorFg(dark) — the light-optimized deep green/red go dim on the dark floor; deleteAccountText error(light)/errorFg(dark) on the stage. Opaque semantic chips unchanged by this pass (tierPill brandSofter, status pills, streak amber, sign-out neutral, severity dots) are text-on-opaque, not text-on-glass, and are not re-declared."
 ],
